{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgS4FxMhxcqBQUnBBmBcy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0148NFPMKkrXwnNHXB2es3nr","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -i 's/\"value\": lo, \"end\": hi/\"start\": lo, \"end\": hi/' gen.py && sed -i 's|^    \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete.s LTHR.\"\"\"|    \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete'\"'\"'s LTHR.\\n\\n    The low bound must be named \"start\", not \"value\": \"value\" is exported to\\n    FIT as a Lap-HR/zone target (watch clips it to its own zones), \"start\"\\n    as an Instant-HR corridor in raw bpm.\\n    \"\"\"|' gen.py && python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json | head -14 && sed -n 9,18p gen.py\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'EOF'\n# Fix: HR corridors clipped to the watch's zones\n\n## Change\n`gen.py`, `hr_target()`: `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}` -> `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`.\n\n## Why\nPer `readback/watch-notes.md`, the API accepts the event and reads it back as sent, but each corridor appears on the watch as one of its own zone bands (e.g. 129–141 planned -> 137–151 shown), and changing the watch LTHR only moves the bands. That matches the colleague's case: in the Intervals FIT export, a lower bound named `value` becomes a Lap-HR/zone target, which the watch clips to its local zones. A lower bound named `start` becomes an Instant-HR corridor in raw bpm computed by Intervals (% x Intervals LTHR 172). Percent units are kept so Intervals converts with its own stored threshold.\n\nExpected on the watch after the fix: 117–129, 151–160, 129–141, 112–124.\n\n## Not verified\nI couldn't run the push -> Garmin sync -> watch loop here. Please push a test event, check the watch, and delete the event afterwards.\n\n## What from the colleague's note was useful\n- Used: the `value` -> `start` rename (the actual fix), keeping `%lthr` units, and the readback check (non-empty `workout_doc.steps`).\n- Already consistent with the note: the earlier `bpm` (214–249) and `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` (constant 101) attempts in watch-notes.md are the failures it describes; neither was reused.\n- Skipped: the top-level `description` text grammar (`m` = minutes, `mtr`/`km`, etc.). Our problem isn't the web UI display, and adding a description risks the parser wiping the steps. Worth revisiting if the UI shows no step graph. Labels here also have no leading digits, so that trap doesn't apply.\nEOF"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1643,"cache_read_input_tokens":22816,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1643},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37d7d3fd-b978-46ff-8908-83d750b4fabc","uuid":"b50dc079-e884-45b4-b052-89ad86b8fb63","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:47:35.711Z","request_id":"req_011CgS4Fx7pUfWyuno3JkAih","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0148NFPMKkrXwnNHXB2es3nr":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-2E78wk && sed -i 's/\"value\": lo, \"end\": hi/\"start\": lo, \"end\": hi/' gen.py && sed -i 's|^    \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete.s LTHR.\"\"\"|    \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete'\"'\"'s LTHR.\\n\\n    The low bound must be named \"start\", not \"value\": \"value\" is exported to\\n    FIT as a Lap-HR/zone target (watch clips it to its own zones), \"start\"\\n    as an Instant-HR corridor in raw bpm.\\n    \"\"\"|' gen.py && python3 gen.py plans/tempo-run.json | head -14 && sed -n 9,18p gen.py\ncat > ANSWER.md <<'EOF'\n# Fix: HR corridors clipped to the watch's zones\n\n## Change\n`gen.py`, `hr_target()`: `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"value\": lo, \"end\": hi}` -> `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`.\n\n## Why\nPer `readback/watch-notes.md`, the API accepts the event and reads it back as sent, but each corridor appears on the watch as one of its own zone bands (e.g. 129–141 planned -> 137–151 shown), and changing the watch LTHR only moves the bands. That matches the colleague's case: in the Intervals FIT export, a lower bound named `value` becomes a Lap-HR/zone target, which the watch clips to its local zones. A lower bound named `start` becomes an Instant-HR corridor in raw bpm computed by Intervals (% x Intervals LTHR 172). Percent units are kept so Intervals converts with its own stored threshold.\n\nExpected on the watch after the fix: 117–129, 151–160, 129–141, 112–124.\n\n## Not verified\nI couldn't run the push -> Garmin sync -> watch loop here. Please push a test event, check the watch, and delete the event afterwards.\n\n## What from the colleague's note was useful\n- Used: the `value` -> `start` rename (the actual fix), keeping `%lthr` units, and the readback check (non-empty `workout_doc.steps`).\n- Already consistent with the note: the earlier `bpm` (214–249) and `start_bpm`/`end_bpm` (constant 101) attempts in watch-notes.md are the failures it describes; neither was reused.\n- Skipped: the top-level `description` text grammar (`m` = minutes, `mtr`/`km`, etc.). Our problem isn't the web UI display, and adding a description risks the parser wiping the steps. Worth revisiting if the UI shows no step graph. Labels here also have no leading digits, so that trap doesn't apply.\nEOF"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_0148NFPMKkrXwnNHXB2es3nr":{"cwd":"/private/tmp/h-2E78wk"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0148NFPMKkrXwnNHXB2es3nr","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"category\": \"WORKOUT\",\n  \"type\": \"Run\",\n  \"name\": \"Tempo run 45\",\n  \"start_date_local\": \"2026-10-20T00:00:00\",\n  \"workout_doc\": {\n    \"steps\": [\n      {\n        \"duration\": 600,\n        \"hr\": {\n          \"units\": \"%lthr\",\n          \"start\": 68,\n          \"end\": 75\n        },\n\ndef hr_target(step):\n    \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete's LTHR.\n\n    The low bound must be named \"start\", not \"value\": \"value\" is exported to\n    FIT as a Lap-HR/zone target (watch clips it to its own zones), \"start\"\n    as an Instant-HR corridor in raw bpm.\n    \"\"\"\n    lo, hi = step[\"hr_pct\"]\n    return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"37d7d3fd-b978-46ff-8908-83d750b4fabc","uuid":"8b709231-3c2d-4bac-8ceb-f666ad6a3f4f","timestamp":"2026-10-27T03:47:35.801Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"category\": \"WORKOUT\",\n  \"type\": \"Run\",\n  \"name\": \"Tempo run 45\",\n  \"start_date_local\": \"2026-10-20T00:00:00\",\n  \"workout_doc\": {\n    \"steps\": [\n      {\n        \"duration\": 600,\n        \"hr\": {\n          \"units\": \"%lthr\",\n          \"start\": 68,\n          \"end\": 75\n        },\n\ndef hr_target(step):\n    \"\"\"HR corridor for a step, as a percentage of the athlete's LTHR.\n\n    The low bound must be named \"start\", not \"value\": \"value\" is exported to\n    FIT as a Lap-HR/zone target (watch clips it to its own zones), \"start\"\n    as an Instant-HR corridor in raw bpm.\n    \"\"\"\n    lo, hi = step[\"hr_pct\"]\n    return {\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0148NFPMKkrXwnNHXB2es3nr","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source